  "prefLabel": "Plc 1406.10 Self-Directed Education",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1406.10 Self-Directed Education.\n\n(a) A licensee may claim credit towards the continuing competence requirement for successful completion of courses that meet the definition of “self-directed education” in Plc 1402, provided that the courses are related to one or more of the NCTRC knowledge domains.\n\n(b) The licensee may claim the same number of hours attributed by the sponsor or provider of the course.\n\n(c) Documentation of a licensee’s successful completion of courses taken through self-directed education shall be a certificate of completion that shows:\n\n(1) The name of the licensee;\n\n(2) The course title and description;\n\n(3) The name and address of the sponsor or provider of the course;\n\n(4) The name and professional credentials of the course instructor;\n\n(5) The number of hours attributed by the sponsor or provider to completion of the course; and\n\n(6) The date the licensee completed the course.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Plc 1400) #13705, eff 8-1-23; ss by #14442, eff 1-26-26, EXPIRES 1-26-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1400.html"
}
